  "details": "If a user has chatboxes disabled entirely or set to \"friends only\" and sees someone typing, it is VERY unclear that they cannot see what they're typing.\n\nSometimes the 3 dots will show up red, but a lot of the time they won't. Even when they do turn red, people just react with \"Whoa! Why is it red? That's weird!\" and then move on.\n\n**Please** consider making this behaviour more obvious and consistent, I want people to see me type and instantly be able to acknowledge that they cannot see my message because they have my chatboxes disabled. The majority of interactions I run into where people have my chatboxes disabled are people who don't even know the chatbox exists. 3 red dots doesn't mean anything to someone who doesn't know how the chatbox works.",
